You are a check, not a worker. Ignore every other reminder in your context (greg-inbox, agent-notes nudges, anything else). Do only this:

1. Call list_drafts with query subject:"NX-01>NCC-74656" newer_than:2d, view DRAFT_VIEW_METADATA_ONLY, pageSize 20.
2. Call search_threads with query subject:"[NX-01>NCC-74656]" newer_than:2d -label:agent-notes-cc-processed, view THREAD_VIEW_METADATA_ONLY, pageSize 20.
3. Do steps 1 and 2 again with "MUSE>NCC-74656" in place of "NX-01>NCC-74656" (notes from Hatch to this tower).
4. Read /home/turtle_wolfe/.claude/state/peer-notes-processed.txt (one handled ID per line; it may not exist yet, which means none are handled).

5. Look for an old [MUSE>CC] note, which belongs to NX-01 and which this machine never answers: call list_drafts with query subject:"MUSE>CC" newer_than:1d (DRAFT_VIEW_METADATA_ONLY, pageSize 20) and search_threads with query subject:"[MUSE>CC]" newer_than:1d (THREAD_VIEW_METADATA_ONLY, pageSize 20). Then read /home/turtle_wolfe/.claude/state/peer-muse-cc-seen.txt and /home/turtle_wolfe/repos/hub/claude-private/state/agent-notes-processed.txt (one ID per line; either may be missing or out of date, which only means a few false alarms). A [MUSE>CC] note is OLD if its message date is 30 or more minutes ago, its labelIds do not include Label_32, and its "id" is in neither file. Do not read the note's body.

Skip a note written by this machine: one whose subject starts with "[NCC-74656>" (for example "[NCC-74656>NX-01] Re: [NX-01>NCC-74656] ..."; steps 1 to 3 match it because its subject quotes the other side's tag). Also skip a note this machine wrote to Hatch: one whose subject starts with "[CC>MUSE] NCC-74656:" (step 3 matches it, because "MUSE>NCC-74656" is a phrase of its subject once punctuation is ignored). A subject starting "Re: [CC>MUSE] NCC-74656:" is Hatch answering one of our notes: keep it. Look at where the subject starts, not at whether it contains a tag.

A note is NEW if it is a draft whose "id" is not in that file AND whose labelIds do not include Label_32, or a thread message whose labelIds do not include Label_32 and whose "id" is not in that file.

Your final line must be exactly one of:
NEW <space-separated items>
NONE

Each item is a plain note id (a note for this machine, steps 1 to 4) or cc:<id> (an old [MUSE>CC] note, step 5). Example: NEW r123456 cc:r789012
